<article class="env-definition" id="0F0Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F0Q">Definition <span data-tag="0F0Q">59.95.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. The <em>cohomological dimension of $X$</em> is the smallest element </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{cd}(X) \in \{ 0, 1, 2, \ldots \}  \cup \{ \infty \}   \]
</div>
  <p> such that for any abelian torsion sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ we have $H^ i_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for $i > \text{cd}(X)$. If $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ we sometimes call this the cohomological dimension of $A$. </p>
</article>